# The Docker build context is the REPO ROOT (docker/unified/build-image.sh
# passes it), because the source has to be COPYed in: the repo is private, so a
# container cannot clone it. Everything below would otherwise be uploaded to the
# daemon on every build.
#
# NOTE: these are NOT gitignore patterns. Docker matches each pattern against
# the whole path from the context root, so a bare `node_modules` excludes only
# a top-level one and misses ui-svelte/node_modules (263 MB). Anything that can
# appear at depth needs the explicit `**/` prefix.

# Build output. build/ alone is 1.5 GB once a packaged bundle with downloaded
# backend binaries lives in it.
build/
**/dist/
**/*.exe
**/*.syso

# Regenerated inside the image by `npm ci` and `vite build`. Copying the host's
# copies in would waste the transfer and risk shipping a stale dashboard.
**/node_modules/
internal/server/ui_dist/
internal/setup/ui_dist/

# 79 MB title model: gitignored, and fetched at runtime from the assets-v1
# release (see internal/server/titlegen_asset.go).
internal/server/assets/*.gguf

# Not needed to compile: version stamping is passed in as a build arg.
.git/
.github/

# Local runtime state and secrets.
**/*.log
**/logs/
**/playground-data/
quartermaster-generate.yaml
quartermaster-overrides.yaml
config.yaml
